WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:05.790
From brutal Gorr the God Butcher scenes, to
Thor dancing to ABBA and the return of the

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:10.090
Grandmaster, there's a stack of deleted scenes
and characters in Thor Love and Thunder!

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:14.170
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing [and explaining]

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:17.270
every scene and character Marvel cut from
the fourth Thor movie.

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:20.039
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:25.210
Christian Bale's Gorr is a creepy, menacing
new antagonist in the MCU, though his presence

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.990
can feel a little lacking in screen time.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:32.809
And in fact, numerous Gorr scenes were filmed
that didn't make the final cut.

00:00:32.809 --> 00:00:38.230
For example, Bale described a horrifying scene
where Gorr, after taking possession of the

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:42.210
Necrosword, cuts away the tattoos on his head
and body that were symbols of his religion.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:46.010
The deleted scene would have explained the
reason for the scars we see on him later in

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:51.470
the movie, but it was removed as it was deemed
too extreme for a family-friendly film.

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:55.560
This shot of Gorr picking up the sword on
a beach which was in the trailers but not

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.960
the final movie could be from that moment.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.770
Bale has also revealed numerous actors he
filmed scenes with that didn't make it into

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:03.770
the final film.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:05.729
I got to work with Peter Dinklage.

00:01:05.729 --> 00:01:10.759
Dinklage played Eitri who last appeared in
Avengers: Infinity War when Thor came to his

00:01:10.759 --> 00:01:13.729
home to ask for a weapon that could kill Thanos.

00:01:13.729 --> 00:01:18.579
That was Stormbreaker, and I suspect the reason
Gorr went to visit Eitri was because the villain

00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:22.359
needed Stormbreaker to open a portal so he
could reach Eternity.

00:01:22.359 --> 00:01:27.439
In the cut scene, Eitri may have been unwilling
or unable to create the weapon again, likely

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:29.310
leading Gorr to kill him.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:33.189
This would have been quite a sad moment as
Eitri was the last of his kind with Thanos

00:01:33.189 --> 00:01:35.469
already having massacred the rest of his people.

00:01:35.469 --> 00:01:37.520
300 dwarves lived on this ring.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.229
I made what he wanted.

00:01:39.229 --> 00:01:40.950
Then he killed everyone anyway.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:44.829
A scene of Gorr killing Eitri might well have
been hard for fans to stomach;

00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:49.340
however, it would certainly have helped beef
up Gorr's screen time and the reasons for

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:50.680
his nickname, the Butcher.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:55.909
And it also looks like Gorr encountered the
Grandmaster from Thor: Ragnarok in the original

00:01:55.909 --> 00:01:57.249
cut of the movie as well.

00:01:57.249 --> 00:01:58.869
I got to work with Jeff Goldblum.

00:01:58.869 --> 00:02:00.679
He's not in the final film either.

00:02:00.679 --> 00:02:03.599
The last time we saw the Grandmaster was in
a Ragnarok post-credit scene on Sakaar where

00:02:03.599 --> 00:02:07.149
he was attempting to bargain with the rebels
who'd risen up against him.

00:02:07.149 --> 00:02:09.240
I just gotta say, I'm proud of you all.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:11.400
This revolution has been a huge success.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.400
Yay us!

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.819
I think it might have been curious to see
how that revolution had panned out for the

00:02:15.819 --> 00:02:21.480
Grandmaster, and whether he'd somehow managed
to charm his way out of a very sticky situation.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.269
I suspect Gorr might have decided to kill
him - even though he's not a god - for his

00:02:25.269 --> 00:02:26.780
tyrannical rule on Sakaar.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:28.300
Doesn't that sound good?

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:32.310
Again, as with Eitri, showing more of Gorr
could have really built up Bale's villain

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:35.160
even further than in the final film.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:40.000
A scene I think a lot of fans wish had been
included was seeing Jane's original transformation

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.780
into the Mighty Thor.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:46.079
Footage from the New Asgard set shows there
was a scene filmed with a dummy and puppeteer

00:02:46.079 --> 00:02:51.060
where Jane was floating in the air and convulsing
right next to the spot where the broken pieces

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.140
of Mjolnir were on display.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:58.530
In the final movie, we do see Jane visiting
the spot and the pieces of the hammer activating,

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:03.359
but we never got to see what happened next,
which presumably involved the hammer re-forming

00:03:03.359 --> 00:03:07.180
itself and Jane becoming Thor for the first
time.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:11.850
Before Russell Crowe became the egotistical
and decadent god Zeus, it appears he was originally

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:13.950
going to play Satan in the movie.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:18.140
A Marvel concept artist has revealed he was
commissioned to create a "comedic" look for

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:19.200
Crowe as Satan.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:24.060
According to the artist, this version of the
devil was meant to be "humourously debauched"

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:27.749
similar to Zeus in the final movie who was
more concerned with his own pleasures than

00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:29.450
helping Thor against Gorr.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:34.840
The devil almost making his first appearance
in the MCU will undoubtedly add fuel to all

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:38.530
the Mephisto theories that have spawned since
WandaVision.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:42.810
Natalie Portman has also revealed there were
tons of scenes involving Jane that didn't

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:46.999
make the final cut and said there's a "missing
period in the film" where we would have seen

00:03:46.999 --> 00:03:50.680
how Jane and Valkyrie got to know each other
and became close.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:54.540
Although Jane dies and goes to Valhalla at
the end of the movie, given the rumours of

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:59.340
a potential Mighty Thor spin-off and how Valkyrie
said to Jane she missed fighting with her

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:04.870
sisters and that she also hoped to go to Valhalla
one day herself, I could see these two teaming

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.750
up in the future.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:10.760
And it looks like Thor originally spent more
time with the Guardians of the Galaxy at the

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:12.029
beginning of the movie.

00:04:12.029 --> 00:04:16.359
This cut scene plays up the idea that Thor
just didn't really want to fight any more

00:04:16.359 --> 00:04:20.859
as the Guardians charge into battle while
he just turns around and walks away with a

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:22.780
resigned air about him.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:27.490
And Thor's deleted voiceover from the first
teaser trailer confirms that, in the original

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:30.840
movie, he was initially done with trying to
be a hero any more.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:32.710
These hands were once used for battle.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.669
Now they're but humble tools for peace.

00:04:34.669 --> 00:04:37.669
I need to figure out exactly who I am.

00:04:37.669 --> 00:04:39.580
My superheroing days are over.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:44.300
A brand new character played by Lena Headey,
perhaps best known to many as Cersei from

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:48.460
Game of Thrones, appeared in scenes filmed
for Thor Love and Thunder which didn't make

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:50.090
it to the final cut.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:54.990
Possible parts she could have played were
an Olympian God, Gorr's wife, or perhaps Valkyrie's

00:04:54.990 --> 00:05:00.210
romantic interest given that at Comic Con,
Tessa Thompson said "as new king of Asgard",

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:03.450
Valkyrie's first order of business would be
to find her queen.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:07.270
Whether Valkyrie's Queen was in the original
script or it was just Thompson's thoughts

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:11.520
about her character at the time, isn't quite
clear at the moment.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:15.161
Chris Hemsworth revealed in an interview that
there was "a full dance scene" of him that

00:05:15.161 --> 00:05:19.639
didn't make it into the final movie, and it
was set to ABBA's "Waterloo".

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:23.370
It also involved Thor "shooting lightning
out of his fingertips" and it could have been

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:28.110
a fun moment, perhaps with shades of Star
Lord's dance-off in the first Guardians movie

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:34.580
mixed with Shazam's "Lightning From My Hands"
scene.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:38.800
Christian Bale has revealed his original request
for taking the part was that he be allowed

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:41.741
to reference Aphex Twin's "Come To Daddy"
music video.

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:44.990
The video has many unsettling elements, and
Bale wanted to emulate a character that emerges

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.970
from a TV set and performs a horrifying scream.

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:52.210
Bale says they did film that moment, but he
understands that it was probably too scary

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:56.639
for a PG-13 movie and said it "might have
had people running for the exits".

00:05:56.639 --> 00:06:01.210
Gorr was also going to have a dance during
his final battle with Thor when he felt like

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:06.159
he was about to win, and the scene would have
taken inspiration from Aphex Twin's "Windowlicker"

00:06:06.159 --> 00:06:10.099
and was also supposed to mirror Thor's earlier
ABBA dance.

00:06:10.099 --> 00:06:14.770
By the sounds of it, it was going to be too
scary or dark as well because in another interview

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:19.389
Bale also said there was a lot more "creepy
as hell stuff, but that was perhaps pushing

00:06:19.389 --> 00:06:23.330
it to a realm where maybe it wouldn't have
been able to be family friendly".

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:27.970
Marvel are well-known for modifying trailer
scenes to remove potential spoilers before

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:28.970
a movie's released.

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:33.569
We saw how Thor's missing eye was restored
for the Ragnarok trailers, and there's a subtle

00:06:33.569 --> 00:06:38.530
change in the Love and Thunder trailers made
to Miek's whiteboard to avoid revealing spoilers.

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:41.080
When Thor gives his rousing speech to the
Asgardians…

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:45.009
Times like this, we need to unite, come together.

00:06:45.009 --> 00:06:46.009
I'm sorry.

00:06:46.009 --> 00:06:50.200
Miek, it's very hard to give a rousing speech
with the [screech sound] noise.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:54.810
…what Miek has written on the whiteboard
in the trailer is basically what's just been

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:56.289
happening in that scene.

00:06:56.289 --> 00:07:00.789
In the final film, however, it's completely
different as the whiteboard has a mass of

00:07:00.789 --> 00:07:04.050
drawings that reveal a huge amount of the
movie's plot;

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:06.879
from Gorr's opening scene to the Guardians
fighting;

00:07:06.879 --> 00:07:09.919
then the gift of the screaming goats;
Sif losing an arm;

00:07:09.919 --> 00:07:13.159
King Valkyrie dreaming of fighting;
Shadow Realm monsters;

00:07:13.159 --> 00:07:15.099
and even Eternity.

00:07:15.099 --> 00:07:19.110
The screaming goats are a running gag in the
movie, though fans are divided on whether

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:21.860
they like them or not.

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:25.669
And according to Tessa Thompson – who's
previously said that she's obsessed with goats

00:07:25.669 --> 00:07:29.440
– she filmed a scene where Valkyrie had
a conversation with the screaming creatures,

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:31.979
but it didn't make it into the final cut.

00:07:31.979 --> 00:07:32.979
Giant goats!

00:07:32.979 --> 00:07:34.259
Oh, look at those!

00:07:34.259 --> 00:07:35.400
They are wonderful.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:37.020
They also scream quite a lot.

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:40.860
There's also some clips in the trailers of
deleted Valkyrie scenes, like this one where

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:44.099
she's licking her sword during the battle
in Omnipotence City.

00:07:44.099 --> 00:07:48.210
And there's another deleted moment of her
bored out of her mind as King Valkyrie, although

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:52.860
a slightly different version where she's twiddling
one of her daggers did make it in to the final

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:53.860
cut.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:57.729
Although these were just tiny deleted moments,
I do wish there'd been a bit more Valkyrie

00:07:57.729 --> 00:08:00.280
in the final film, and less Korg.

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:04.349
In Ragnarok, he was fine as comic relief in
a few scenes, but in Love and Thunder, it

00:08:04.349 --> 00:08:08.560
felt like he was in too much of the movie
and his jokes often didn't land for me, though,

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:10.750
of course, comedy is very subjective.

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:15.520
There were also some more emotional scenes
between Jane and Thor removed from the final

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:16.520
cut.

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:20.500
And Portman has also said there were "20 different
versions of [one key scene]".

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:25.259
As you see, lots of stuff ends up on the cutting
room floor, even though it is brilliant, beautiful

00:08:25.259 --> 00:08:26.259
stuff.

00:08:26.259 --> 00:08:30.689
Portman also revealed that there are "whole
sequences, planets, characters, and worlds

00:08:30.689 --> 00:08:32.610
that didn't end up in the movie".

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:36.700
The trailers do have some deleted shots of
Valkyrie together with Thor on a planet with

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:41.090
what looks like a lot of trash behind them
which might mean they went back to Sakaar

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:42.530
at some point.

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:46.570
Of course, with all of these deleted scenes,
a lot of fans will be asking for The Waititi

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:52.080
Cut, which apparently was initially four hours
long, versus the final cut of just under two

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:53.080
hours.

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:58.730
Now, this 4-hour cut was never an actual watchable
movie, it's what's known as the assembly cut

00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:03.030
which is all of the main footage which might
make it into the final film before the director

00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:04.930
and editor begin trimming it down.

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:09.760
In fact, as much as I wish some things had
been in the final movie like Jane's Mighty

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:15.150
Thor transformation, more Valkyrie and more
Gorr, it's essential for any movie to trim

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:18.030
the fat and cut out unnecessary subplots.

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:21.710
So, do you think Love and Thunder did a good
job of doing that?

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:25.330
Or did it feel "like [they] asked a bunch
of 10 year olds what should be in a movie

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:29.980
and just said yes to everything", which is
what Taika Waititi said himself it felt like

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:31.870
when they were developing the film?

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:35.950
It's always fascinating to know why things
make it into a movie and what gets cut out

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:40.460
for better or worse, and if you'd like to
discover the horrific original opening scene

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:44.851
of Scarlet Witch murdering Mordo in Doctor
Strange in the Multiverse of Madness, tap

00:09:44.851 --> 00:09:47.580
here for everything that was deleted from
that movie.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:49.590
There's also a link in the video description.

00:09:49.590 --> 00:09:52.760
So, how do you rate Thor Love and Thunder?

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:55.730
And do you wish any of these deleted scenes
had been in the final movie?

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:58.100
Let me know in the comments below.

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:01.790
And if you enjoyed this video, do leave a
thumbs-up, I really appreciate it.

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:06.790
Tap left for my full Marvel deleted scenes
playlist including how Black Widow almost

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.270
came back from the dead.

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:11.540
Thanks for watching and hope you have a marvellous
movie-loving week!

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:13.040
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

